1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,928
Welcome to Frog Bot. It is a desktop app where AI agents work like
teammates on your computer.

2
00:00:07,628 --> 00:00:19,471
The first time you open Frog Bot, it asks for an API key from Claude
or OpenAI. Then you can start
chatting with Frog right away.

3
00:00:20,171 --> 00:00:29,049
This is the main home screen. Your agents and groups are on the left,
the chat is in the middle, and quick suggestions help you begin.

4
00:00:29,749 --> 00:00:40,487
Use the plus button to add a new agent. Give the agent a name, an
emoji, a color, a simple role, and plain instructions for how it
should help.

5
00:00:41,187 --> 00:00:49,895
You can also create group chats with more than one agent. In a group,
type @Name when you want to speak to one specific teammate.

6
00:00:50,595 --> 00:01:02,227
Chat with Frog the same way you would chat with a coworker. Agents can
read and write files, research the web, use a browser, run commands,
and ask other agents for help.

7
00:01:02,927 --> 00:01:14,195
When an agent wants to do something important, Frog Bot asks first.
You can allow it, say no, open details, or stop the work at the top of
the chat.

8
00:01:14,895 --> 00:01:24,277
After you approve an action, the agent continues and reports what
happened. This keeps you in control while still letting the team do
real work.

9
00:01:24,977 --> 00:01:36,635
The About panel shows how an agent is set up. You can edit its name
and instructions, choose its brain, pick which apps it can use, and
decide whether it can work on its own.

10
00:01:37,335 --> 00:01:45,338
The Screen tab lets you monitor the agent's computer. You can see its
live steps, so you always know what it is doing.

11
00:01:46,038 --> 00:01:58,920
Integrations connect Frog Bot to the tools you already use. You can
use the built-in browser, and add apps like Slack, Notion, GitHub,
Linear, or custom apps.

12
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:08,723
To add another app, fill in the server address and a token if one is
needed. Then click Add, and the app becomes available to your agents.

13
00:02:09,423 --> 00:02:17,816
The Logs tab shows a live record of everything that happens. You can
filter it, copy it, or save it when you need to review the work.

14
00:02:18,516 --> 00:02:30,854
Settings are where you manage the basics. You can update your API key,
team name, default brain, startup options, screen learning, and where
files are stored.

15
00:02:31,554 --> 00:02:41,492
That is the flow of Frog Bot. Create agents, give them work, watch
their progress, connect your apps, and find shared files whenever you
need them.
